From: uDroid graphics runtime
Subject: [PATCH] libhybris: isolate Android Q TLS in a preloaded static reserve

Android vendor libraries use Bionic's thread-pointer-relative TLS relocations.
Resolving those offsets against glibc corrupts the host thread and made
multi-threaded compositors slow down or crash.

Reserve 64 KiB of initial-exec glibc TLS in the preloaded bridge and relocate
Bionic TPREL and TLSDESC references into that block. Finish the embedded
linker's startup TLS set before Android constructors run, initialize the main
thread, and interpose host pthread creation so later Linux and Android workers
receive the same isolated layout.

Keep dynamic TLS resolution inside the Android namespace, repair the shadowed
allocation and disabled frees in the imported Q implementation, and use the
Android Q ABI constants instead of the host limits. HYBRIS_TLS_PRELOAD selects
the first Android library graph that must be loaded before main; launchers must
set it to their validated vendor root library and preload libhybris-common.

The final eight bytes of the fixed reserve hold the per-thread initialization
generation. The linker aborts if the Android layout exceeds the remaining
capacity rather than placing it over glibc TLS.
